Package: dtaparser
Title: Native Reader for Stata DTA Files
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Bearak", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "jbearak@guttmacher.org")
Description: Reads Stata DTA files through the repository's native Rust
    parser. Numeric and character vectors are populated directly by compiled
    code while retaining dataset labels, variable labels, display formats,
    value labels, temporal classes, and Stata tagged missing values.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    dplyr (>= 1.1.0),
    readr (>= 2.2.0),
    rlang,
    tibble,
    tidyselect,
    vctrs
Suggests:
    callr,
    haven,
    httpuv,
    testthat (>= 3.1.7)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Cargo and Rust >= 1.98.0; on Windows, the Rust target matching
    R (x86_64-pc-windows-gnu for x86_64 R or
    aarch64-pc-windows-gnullvm for aarch64 R)
NeedsCompilation: yes
